NOTE ON SCOPE

This license applies to everything under AntiHackerXVerify/ and only to that
directory. The rest of the AntiHackerX repository is licensed under GNU GPL
v3.0 only; see ../LICENSE.

Why this module is permissive: it is a standalone example showing what a packed
program looks like, and it carries the copyright-notice snippet that AntiHackerX
users embed into their own programs. Keeping it MIT means you can copy from it
into a proprietary program without GPL-3.0 terms applying to that program.

Nothing here links against AntiHackerX or against native-obfuscator; the only
dependencies are JDK classes (java.awt / java.util / javax.swing).

The programs you *build* with AntiHackerX are unaffected by either license:
whatever native-obfuscator emits into your output directory is governed by the
Output Exception in that project's LICENSE, not by this file.
